  "body": "Found during #1953. Not confirmed as a defect.\n\nAt the harness size of 1280 x 720, the Properties leaf is `[990, 82] - [1264, 682]`. On some pages, the AccessKit rect of a widget is past the right edge of the leaf:\n\n| Page | Widget | Rect x range |\n|---|---|---|\n| Model (`Block`) | `Set` (next to \"STEP facet budget\") | 1266-1293 |\n| Operation (`Contour1`) | `×` (origin row) | 1407-1422 |\n| Operation (`Contour1`) | `Delete operation` | 1315-1422 |\n| Setup settings | `Pick for WCS` | 1282-1361 |\n| Setup tool list | `Edit` | 1294-1325 |\n| Tool library | last `Add` rows | up to 1334 |\n\nThe page may scroll across, or the widget may be clipped and not visible to the user. Do this:\n1. Open each page at 1280 x 720 and find out if the user can see and reach the widget.\n2. If the user cannot reach it, raise this issue to `P3` and fix the row so that it fits the pane.\n3. If the page scrolls across on purpose, close this issue with that reason.\n\nThe readings come from a probe over the AccessKit tree on `origin/main` at `cda3d5896`.\n",
